# CrossGuild Architecture Rules

Reference: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`

## Pages must be thin

- `src/app/**/page.tsx` → metadata + `<XxxView />` from `@/features/X/views/` (~15 lines max)
- No business logic, data fetching, or large JSX in page files

## Route handlers must be thin

- `src/app/api/**/route.ts` → auth wrapper + validation + call to `@/features/X/server/X.server.ts`
- **Never put Prisma queries directly in `route.ts`**

## Feature structure

Each domain under `src/features/X/`:

```
components/  hooks/  services/  server/  validations/  views/  types/
```

## Naming suffixes

| Suffix | Role |
|--------|------|
| `.view.tsx` | Page-level view |
| `.component.tsx` | UI component |
| `.hook.ts` | React hook |
| `.service.ts` | Client API calls |
| `.server.ts` | Server/Prisma logic |
| `.schema.ts` | Zod validation |
| `.type.ts` | TypeScript types |

## Import rules

- Use `@/` path alias (`@/*` → `./src/*`)
- Features import from `@/shared/` only — never from other features
- `src/shared/` must not import from `src/features/`

## Example: thin page

```tsx
import CartView from "@/features/cart/views/cart.view";

export default function CartPage() {
  return <CartView />;
}
```

## Example: thin route

```typescript
import { getCart } from "@/features/cart/server/cart.server";

export const GET = withAuth(async (_req, { session }) => {
  const items = await getCart(session.user.id);
  return apiSuccess({ items });
});
```
